    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a high-ceiling schedule today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88), who stands as our clear anchor against Brown. His elite scoring is driven by a strong platoon advantage and a favorable matchup against a 4.53 xERA arm. Alongside him, **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Nasim Nunez** (67.37) provide significant upside; both benefit from a target-rich environment against the porous pitching of Lopez, with **Nasim Nunez** buoyed by an attractive park factor and SP weakness that elevates his utility despite a lower batting order slot. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (66.12) similarly exploits this matchup, and we are banking on his confirmed placement at the top of the order to capitalize on the 5.64 xERA projected for the opposition.\n\nEfficiency remains the primary constraint for our roster, forcing a difficult decision regarding **Curtis Mead** (58.98). While **Curtis Mead** carries a strong score driven by a park boost and the same favorable matchup as our other infielders, he sits on the bench because our depth at MI and 2B\u2014specifically the higher-scoring profiles of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Nasim Nunez**\u2014pushed him just outside the active threshold. Further down the sheet, we have opted to keep **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (54.37) in reserve as his profile currently yields less value than the projected efficiency of **Kyle Tucker** (53.64) or the high-floor utility play of **Jacob Wilson** (60.32).\n\nRisk management remains a focus as we monitor **Jackson Merrill** (54.46), who carries a 38% rain probability warning. While his skill set remains viable, the weather risk combined with a difficult matchup against Cameron slightly tempers expectations. Conversely, we are navigating the difficulty of the Schlittler matchup for **Andy Pages** (49.57) and **Kyle Tucker** (53.64); while their base projections are solid, their scores are suppressed by the opposing pitcher's ability to limit production. We will continue to monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Nasim Nunez**, as any shuffle in their batting order could necessitate a late-game rotation update to maintain our optimal 5x5 output.",
